######################################################
######   COMBAT BOSS AUTHORING GUIDE
######################################################

== 1. THE FRAMEWORK ==

  POD_combat_initialize_boss_effect = { TIER = <1..3> }
      Character scope. Sets the pod_combat_boss character flag and stores pod_combat_boss_tier.
      Tier bonuses are shared script values: health +5 per tier before the 20-box cap
      (pod_combat_boss_health_bonus_value) and AP +0 / +3 / +6 (pod_combat_boss_ap_bonus_value,
      applied through pod_combat_ap_modifier_value). Reapplying replaces the tier.

  POD_combat_boss_grant_move_effect = { MOVE = <DECISION key> }
      Character scope. Adds the registered move story to the character's pod_combat_boss_moves
      list. The shared BOSS rule in pod_combat_actor_unlocks_move_trigger admits the
      granted moves. Grant in the template's after_creation. If the move is not
      in the save's catalogue the effect writes a debug.log line naming the key.

  POD_combat_launch_boss_effect = { TEMPLATE TITLE TEAM_NAME FATALITY OUTPUT_EVENT INCLUDE_COTERIE MUSIC DESPAWN }
      Human host scope. creates the boss from TEMPLATE, registers it with combat 
      cleanup when DESPAWN = yes, seats it as the enemy, seats every available
      coterie member when INCLUDE_COTERIE = yes, applies TITLE / TEAM_NAME,
      finalizes, and cues MUSIC. All eight parameters are required. On failure it posts the
      pod_combat_boss_launch_unavailable toast and removes an unseated spawns AI.
      FATALITY: practice | no | possible | default | always (see COMBAT_DUEL_BUILDER_GUIDE.info).
      OUTPUT_EVENT: pod_combat_debug.0001 posts the standard victory / defeat / draw toasts.
      MUSIC: any key from music/in_game, for example mood_carthago_delenda_est.

  POD_combat_boss_finish_creation_effect
      Character scope, runs once. The end of the creation pipeline: PoD's lifestyle initializer, 
      energy, masquerade, resonance for vampires, and had_POD_character_initialization. It is 
      reached from the on_character_created hook in common/on_action/pod_combat_boss_on_actions.txt 
      for any created character that already carries the pod_combat_boss flag.

  POD_combat_boss_grant_unlimited_energy_effect
      Character scope, opt-in. Adds the modifier pod_combat_boss_unlimited_energy_modifier.
      POD_has_infinite_blood_trigger, accepts it, so every blood cost is free, in and out of
      combat, and the AI stops rationing energy moves. PoD has that rule for hunger splats 
      only; on another splat the effect logs and grantsnothing. The modifier shows on the
      character as Boundless Vitae and stays with a boss kept through DESPAWN = no.

  The BOSS move category is handled once: hidden from the loadout editor and the sheet 
  (including show-all), refused by human unlock trigger and presets.

== 2. ADD A BOSS ==

  a. Template (common/scripted_character_templates/). Traits, skills, culture, faith, prowess.
     after_creation runs in the new character's scope and holds identity and authored stats only:
         set_immortal_age = 30
         POD_combat_initialize_boss_effect = { TIER = 3 }
         POD_combat_boss_grant_move_effect = { MOVE = POD_combat_move_<key> }   # one line per move
         POD_combat_boss_grant_unlimited_energy_effect = yes                  # optional
     Energy, masquerade, resonance, the lifestyle trees and the initialization flag come from
     POD_combat_boss_finish_creation_effect through the creation hook.
     See POD_combat_troile_debug_template and POD_combat_troile_debug_initialize_effect for a
     generation-three vampire. Appearance can be copied from a history character with
     copy_inheritable_appearance_from.

  b. Registry block, in POD_initialize_combat_moves (pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt), inside
     the BOSS MOVES block at the end of the registry. Same constructor as any move:
         POD_init_combat_move = {
             DECISION   = POD_combat_move_<key>
             SKILL_KEY  = <key>
             CATEGORY   = BOSS
             CONFIG     = boss_<name>
             GROUP      = vampire           # the splat family the move belongs to
             AP_COST    = @ap_cost_major
             AI_WEIGHT  = 20                # 8..20 is the catalogue range; 80 forces the move every turn
             TARGETING  = single_enemy
         }
         scope:new_combat_move = { ...setters... }
     CONFIG only needs to be unique per boss; the unlock dispatcher has no branch for it.

  c. Decision (common/decisions/POD_Combat/pod_combat_boss_move_decisions.txt), one per move:
         POD_combat_move_<key> = {
             picture = { reference = @texture_celerity }
             is_valid_showing_failures_only = {
                 custom_tooltip = {
                     text = pod_combat_req_boss_move
                     pod_combat_boss_move_granted_trigger = { STORY = character:POD_wraith_01.var:POD_combat_move_<key> }
                 }
             }
             decision_group_type = hidden ai_check_interval = 0 confirm_text = blank_line
         }

  d. Localization: POD_combat_move_<key> (name), POD_combat_move_<key>_desc
     ("[PODCombatMoveDesc('POD_combat_move_<key>')]"), POD_combat_move_<key>_tooltip (flavor),
     plus the fight title and team-name keys the launch call uses.

  e. Call POD_combat_launch_boss_effect (events/POD_combat_troile_debug_events.txt):
         option = {
             name = pod_combat_boss_debug.0001.<name>
             custom_tooltip = pod_combat_duel_begins_tt
             hidden_effect = {
                 POD_combat_launch_boss_effect = { TEMPLATE = ... TITLE = ... TEAM_NAME = ...
                     FATALITY = practice OUTPUT_EVENT = pod_combat_debug.0001
                     INCLUDE_COTERIE = yes MUSIC = ... DESPAWN = yes }
             }
         }
